# An error is a value (#138): `throw new Error(..)` builds one in the arm that throws it, the error an arm hands on is one
# value at the choice's moment, and each border it crosses uncaught hands it on, up to the route. `parseLine` is handed to
# `map`, so what it throws `parse` hands on.
